# Using axi wdata without wvalid qualification in TLUL

- Source URL: https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-ss/issues/535

Hi Caliptra team,
        In Caliptra SS simulation, we encounter X value issue. By tracing the code, we found that there could be an issue  in the RTL code: caliptra-ss-main/src/tlul/rtl/tlul_cmd_ingt_chk.sv ( line 44 ).


![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c0ae44cc-8335-4501-8b44-e8aec0334985)

The issue is using "data_err" without checking qualification of AXI wvalid. "tl_i.a_valid" is from AXI awvalid or arvalid, but "data_err" is from AXI wdata, so there could be scenerio when AXI arvalid == 1, but wvalid == 0, wdata is unknown.


        Could you help to check whether this is a real issue ?


Best Regards
Derek Wang

